    <div class="teaser">
      <h3 id="housing-the-homeless">Housing the Homeless</h3>
      <p class="article-subtitle">
        Does investing in permanent housing for the homeless significantly
        decrease homelessness?
      </p>
      <p class="article-date">
        <time datetime="2020-10-25">October 25, 2020</time>
      </p>

      <p>
        I analyzed the most recent available data on homelessness in the United
        States, collected and provided by the Department of Housing and Urban
        Development (HUD), to ask whether a state's investment in permanent
        supportive housing significantly decreases the number of homeless people
        in that state.
      </p>

      <p>
        Comparing point-in-time counts against housing inventory counts from
        2007 to 2019, the states that invested most heavily in permanent
        supportive housing were the states where homelessness fell, and an
        independent t-test put the result below the 0.05 significance level.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/projects/housing-the-homeless"
          >Read the full analysis &rarr;</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
